    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12.x\n\n### Description\n\n```html\n<span\n>asdf</span\n>\n```\n\nThis is valid HTML, but `vit` doesn't recognize that span is a tag. Instead of selecting `asdf` it selects the whole thing.\n\nFor ref:\n\nhttps://w3c.github.io/html-reference/syntax.html#syntax-elements\n\n> End tags consist of the following parts, in exactly the following order:\n> - A \"<\" character.\n> - A \"/\" character\n> - The element’s [tag name](https://w3c.github.io/html-reference/syntax.html#tag-name).\n> - **Optionally, one or more [space characters](https://w3c.github.io/html-reference/terminology.html#space).**\n> - A \">\" character.\n\n### Reproduction\n\n- Add whitespace before `>` in closing tag `</span >`\n- Try to do an `it` cmd\n- Span isn't recognized as a tag",
